{"animath":"0.1","canvas":{"height":540,"width":960},"kind":"concept","level":"secondary","scenes":[{"caption":"A right-angled triangle","duration_ms":7000,"id":"s1","narration":"Take a right-angled triangle with short sides 3 and 4. Pythagoras says the square on the longest side equals the sum of the squares on the other two.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"legA","kind":"line","stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":4,"x1":300,"x2":300,"y1":340,"y2":220}},{"at_ms":500,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"legB","kind":"line","stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":4,"x1":300,"x2":460,"y1":340,"y2":340}},{"at_ms":1000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"hyp","kind":"line","stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":4,"x1":300,"x2":460,"y1":220,"y2":340}},{"at_ms":1600,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"none","h":24,"id":"ra","kind":"rect","stroke":"#1a1a1a","strokeWidth":2,"w":24,"x":300,"y":316}},{"at_ms":2200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"la","kind":"text","size":28,"text":"a = 3","x":258,"y":290}},{"at_ms":2800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"lb","kind":"text","size":28,"text":"b = 4","x":360,"y":380}},{"at_ms":3400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"lc","kind":"text","size":28,"text":"c = ?","x":400,"y":260}}]},{"caption":"Squares on the short sides","duration_ms":8000,"id":"s2","narration":"Build a square on each short side. Their areas are 3 squared, which is 9, and 4 squared, which is 16.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"legA","kind":"line","stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":4,"x1":300,"x2":300,"y1":340,"y2":220}},{"at_ms":100,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"legB","kind":"line","stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":4,"x1":300,"x2":460,"y1":340,"y2":340}},{"at_ms":200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"hyp","kind":"line","stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":4,"x1":300,"x2":460,"y1":220,"y2":340}},{"at_ms":1000,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#e8f0fe","h":120,"id":"sqA","kind":"rect","stroke":"#2b5cb8","strokeWidth":3,"w":120,"x":180,"y":220}},{"at_ms":2000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"tA","kind":"text","size":28,"text":"3² = 9","x":196,"y":290}},{"at_ms":3200,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#e8f0fe","h":160,"id":"sqB","kind":"rect","stroke":"#2b5cb8","strokeWidth":3,"w":160,"x":300,"y":340}},{"at_ms":4200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"tB","kind":"text","size":28,"text":"4² = 16","x":326,"y":425}}]},{"caption":"The square on the hypotenuse","duration_ms":8000,"id":"s3","narration":"Now the square on the longest side, c. Its area must equal 9 plus 16.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"legA","kind":"line","stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":4,"x1":300,"x2":300,"y1":340,"y2":220}},{"at_ms":100,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"legB","kind":"line","stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":4,"x1":300,"x2":460,"y1":340,"y2":340}},{"at_ms":200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"hyp","kind":"line","stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":4,"x1":300,"x2":460,"y1":220,"y2":340}},{"at_ms":1200,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#fef3e2","id":"sqC","kind":"polygon","points":[[300,220],[460,340],[580,180],[420,60]],"stroke":"#b86a1f","strokeWidth":3}},{"at_ms":2800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"tC","kind":"text","size":30,"text":"c² = ?","x":620,"y":200}},{"at_ms":4500,"do":"emphasize","dur_ms":1000,"target":"sqC"}]},{"caption":"9 + 16 = 25","duration_ms":7000,"id":"s4","narration":"Nine plus sixteen is twenty-five, so c squared is 25 and c is 5. That is Pythagoras: a squared plus b squared equals c squared.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"eq1","kind":"text","size":36,"text":"3² + 4² = 9 + 16 = 25","x":240,"y":200}},{"at_ms":1800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"eq2","kind":"text","size":36,"text":"c² = 25   →   c = 5","x":240,"y":280}},{"at_ms":3600,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#1f7a3a","id":"rule","kind":"latex","size":46,"tex":"a^2 + b^2 = c^2","x":240,"y":390}},{"at_ms":5200,"do":"emphasize","dur_ms":1000,"target":"rule"}]}],"subject":"math","title":"Pythagoras' theorem: a² + b² = c²","topic":"e-trigonometry"}